00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.310 align:start position:0%
 
working in a morgue requires some  specific skills you need to be  comfortable being around the dad you  need to have a great attention to detail  and you better not be squeamish you'll  be getting up close and personal with  some gruesome specimens but for those  who find themselves in a specific morgue  under the supervision of the scp  foundation they'll need to have some  extra specific skills if they hope to  get out alive  in the basement of an old hospital in  great britain there was a morgue it  appeared like any other until the 1980s  with a busy hospital staff coming in and  out to investigate causes of death and  perform autopsies reporting anything  unique to the doctors upstairs but soon  the morgue and the hospital around it  began to get a reputation people  whispered that something wasn't right in  the morgue that there were supernatural  dealings afoot and soon  they were proven right because what's  dead in  scp-022 doesn't always stay dead the  foundation soon stepped in and  quarantined the morgue condemning the  building an investigation didn't find  any cause for the unpredictable and  dangerous phenomena but the foundation  was able to track the pattern of  reanimations and did happen upon the  following the morgue is filled with body  storage drawers and at random times the  spontaneous opening of one or several of  them will occur and despite the fact  that the morgue has been out of  operation for quite a long while  whenever a drawer opens there is a body  laying inside under a sheet every time  and after six minutes of being opened  the body will wake up when awake these  reanimated corpses have exactly one  mission to get out of the morgue by any  means necessary if the corpse is  relatively intact it will leap off the  table and charge at the door and  anything else in its way while no  specimen has ever been safely captured  for testing their base strength seems to  be far stronger than any normal human no  evidence of what gives them this power  has been found but they are absolutely  formidable and very hard to stop and to  add to the difficulty they're even  harder to kill a second time around  while all evidence indicates that these  are reanimated humans they do not seem  to be limited by the same physical  effects of damage those who have tried  to stop these undead beings from getting  to the door have found this out the hard  way these cadavers seem to be immune to  just about any form of impairment their  bodies don't give off heat and they do  not need to eat drink or breathe if  their bodies are severely damaged the  body part with the greatest mass stays  active and doesn't seem to slow down at  all only one thing actually seems to  impede upon the horrifying persistence  that these cadavers portray in their  attempts to escape  fire the foundation has discovered that  fire may be the one effective way of  stopping the undead specimens but it's  not as easy as simply setting them on  fire high powered fire is needed to  incinerate their tissue and render them  little more than a pile of ash the good  news is there is another method to  neutralize them and that's to weight  them out if the corpse is active but  contained by the foundation's security  they will eventually expire when  whatever power is animating them finally  runs out but this can take between two  days and three weeks which can be  problematic if they're joined by other  friends from the drawers but not all of  the living corpses follow the same  pattern bodies emerge in the drawers  seemingly at random and the state they  arrive in is just as unpredictable this  may correspond to how they died and an  investigation is ongoing in regards to  how these corpses wind up in the morgue  to begin with some arrive in good shape  as if they were recently deceased from a  heart attack or other similar ailment  these are the most dangerous specimens  others may be decomposed or damaged  which will cause them to be slower but  some are in such poor condition that  they can't get up off the slab at all  and that's where scp-022 reacts in an  unexpected way the cadaver may be too  damaged to move but it's still  reanimated and will struggle and twitch  on the slab for whatever the duration is  of their reanimated life but if it  expires while still on the slab the slab  will act on its own and slide back into  the drawer with the cadaver still on it  the body then disappears and from what  witnesses have reported a smell of  burning tissue similar to cremation then  fills the air in the morgue no one knows  where the corpses go but perhaps more  importantly where do they come from that  is the one question that concerns the  foundation the most about scp-022  while the main priority is to contain  the reanimated corpses studying them is  also vital unfortunately testing on the  reanimated is limited due to their  aggressive nature however agents have  been able to observe them just enough to  describe them and send the descriptions  out to law enforcement as evidence shows  that scp-022 may also be able to reach  outside of the confines of the morgue  what the foundation has learned from  interfacing with local law enforcement  is that every single one resembles a  corpse stolen from a morgue around the  country studies of the specimens after  they expire if not consumed by the  drawers is the easiest way to conduct  testing they can be examined safely and  appear to be standard human corpses with  the only exception being any damage done  during the attempt by the foundation to  contain them they don't seem to have any  unusual organs or chemicals in the body  and no explanation for their reanimation  can be found there is however one other  element of  scp-022 that concerns researchers  nothing seems to be able to be added to  the morgue when something is placed into  or enters the room it vanishes after  only seconds this has happened to  inanimate objects as well as to animals  and even to people there is no evidence  as to where these specimens go what  makes this happen is unknown but  provides further evidence for the theory  that there is definitely some dangerous  anomaly governing scp-022  far beyond the fact corpses are simply  reanimating while the rest of the  hospital that contains scp-022 has so  far been free of anomalies and is a  standard abandoned building an  exploration of the room above the morgue  revealed something concerning in the  room agents discovered a massive pile of  matter that seemed to be composed of all  the things that had vanished upon  entering  scp-022 all of the metal objects had  been broken down and the organic  material had decomposed everything  looked like it had been there far longer  than the time since it had vanished  despite appearing only three minutes  after its disappearance and testing but  one thing was missing from the mystery  pile what happened to the people who had  disappeared inside the morgue none of  the humans who disappeared either in  accidents before the foundation stepped  in or in testing appeared in the pile in  decayed form but it wasn't long before  they appeared in another way the  foundation observed that several of the  corpses that appeared from behind the  drawers of scp-022  resembled the unfortunate citizens who  had disappeared into the room in the  past the morgue's victims had returned  and they wanted out now it was clear  that the priority had to be containment  the door to the facility was destroyed  during a security breach by a  particularly tenacious specimen so the  foundation installed a more powerful  vault door shortly after taking over the  facility with orders that it must remain  locked at all times because of the  morgue's ability to absorb anything that  enters it containment of the entities is  dependent entirely on automated systems  if the cadavers happen to make it  through the vault door placed just  outside of the perimeter of the original  scp-022 room awaiting their arrival are  the foundation's high-powered automated  fire weapons once the undead cross the  threshold of the door the weapons are  triggered and incinerate them  immediately it is only if this system  fails that response teams are sent in to  contain the threat followed by cleanup  crews no humans are to enter scp-022  unless further testing is needed nor is  any entity to be removed from the  containment site while the first time  the foundation encountered one of the  reanimated corpses it had been  immediately destroyed the second time  was a different story it appeared to be  an asian man in his 50s and its body was  mostly intact with the exception of a  large chest scar that resembled that of  an autopsy it claimed its name was john  and remembered dying in a car accident  but it refused to admit that it was dead  then it saw its reflection and things  took a disturbing turn while the  specimen had remained calm until then it  became extremely angry as soon as it saw  its image on the steel table and had to  be restrained while in containment it  claimed over and over again that it was  not the man it saw in its reflection  whoever was in the body didn't believe  it was the older asian man  it then became enraged screaming and  smashing its head against a wall until  it stopped talking and eventually  stopped moving all together no more  information could be obtained what was  scp-022 doing to the people who appeared  in it the answer to that question became  a little clearer after the foundation  was able to capture a specimen again  this time it was shortly after a d-class  designated  d-5619 had been sent into the morgue and  immediately disappeared what emerged  from the drawers shortly thereafter  though wasn't the d-class it was a  little girl who looked to be about 12  years old and just like the cadaver  captured prior when restrained it became  extremely angry however it did  eventually cooperate in answering  questions for the foundation it was soon  identified as d 5619  the unfortunate d-class testing victim  it wasn't long after the question of  what had happened to d 5619's body was  answered  three weeks following the incident d  5619's body was returned from the  drawers but it wasn't him inside of it a  brief interview confirmed that this was  a very confused but overall cooperative  89 year old woman in the body of the  d-class whatever effect is going on  within scp-022  it seems to return people in twisted  mismatched combinations of body and mind  the foundation is still investigating  exactly what is happening inside of  scp-022 with a focus on how the anomaly  gets its corpses from around great  britain but when dealing with the  mystery morgue itself the foundation  holds to a simple rule nothing gets in  and nothing gets out for more on a  mysterious thread in an unlikely place  check out  scp-974 treehouse predator or check out  this other video instead for more from  scp explained

